# Cloudflare Pages serving order, for reference:
#   1. Pages Functions (functions/) -- _redirects is never consulted for those
#   2. a matching static file, which includes every prerendered route
#   3. the rewrites below
#   4. 404.html, served with a real 404 status
#
# There is deliberately NO "/*  /index.html  200" catch-all. With one, every
# path on the domain answered 200 with the 20kB app shell -- /.git/config,
# /root/.git-credentials, /application-prod.properties and ~40 other probes
# from one scanner all got HTTP 200 (97.5% of its 4,759 requests in the three
# days to 26 Aug 2026). Nothing leaked; it is the shell, not the file. But a
# domain that answers 200 to everything reports no 404s, which is a soft-404
# farm for Google and a green light for the scanners.
#
# So the rewrites are enumerated instead. Prerendered routes
# (scripts/prerender.mjs) need no entry -- they are real files on disk. Only
# client-only routes do. Add a route to src/main.jsx that is not prerendered
# and you must add it here; test/spa-routing.test.mjs fails if you forget.
# The target is /app-shell (dist/app-shell.html, written by prerender.mjs) and
# NOT /index.html: Pages normalises "/index.html" to "/" and a rewrite whose
# destination is itself redirected answers with that 308 instead of the page.
/admin         /app-shell  200
/order/*       /app-shell  200
/alerts/*      /app-shell  200
/es/alerts/*   /app-shell  200
